{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["And showing steadfast love to thousands — to children: thirtieths, fourths, twentieths, tenths, hundreds, and thousands of children; 'thousands' means a thousand generations. And the verses do not contradict each other according to the plain sense: here it speaks of children and grandchildren — all children are one generation, and their children's children are a second generation, and the children of the last generation. The last of the thousand [generations] are called 'children' — 'children to thousands' — whereas in Deuteronomy, which does not mention 'children' nor 'thirty' nor 'fourths,' as it is written there: ״וְיָדַעְתָּ כִּי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ הוּא הָאֱלֹהִים״ and so forth, ״לְאֹהֲבָיו וּלְשֹׁמְרֵי מִצְוֺתָיו לְאֶלֶף דּוֹר״ — and that 'thousand' is 'children to thousands.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The terms שלשים רבעים חמשיים עשיריים denote fractional degrees of descent (thirtieths, fourths, twentieths, tenths); the phrase בנים אלפים הם אלף דור is rendered hyper-literally as the text stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:15.658322684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}